From 95acec32065b868f42d798cbf10312252c56192c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:22:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 831/831] perf(worker): synchronize TP ranks and pause cyclic
 GC across engine_grid timed replays

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 (series 0001..0830).
Upstream status: local candidate-63 patch for TP boot-to-boot grid variance.
Quality implications: none; engine_grid profiling harness only, zero serving or numerical changes.

Rationale:
4-rank Torch Profiler traces showed multi-millisecond host/rank arrival skew on
one rank causing the other three ranks to spin inside oneshot_allreduce_kernel.
In GPUModelRunner.engine_grid(), drain the GPU stream, run gc.collect(), and
barrier all TP ranks on tp_group.cpu_group between warmup and the timed loop,
then pause cyclic GC across the timed replay loop (restoring GC state in
finally) so asynchronous per-rank GC pauses cannot skew collective arrivals.

Tests:
- pytest --noconftest tests/v1/worker/test_engine_grid_sync.py (2 passed).
